---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DesignTodo from './DesignTodo.astro';
import '../styles/okhosting.css';
import '../styles/okhosting-2026.css';
const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const es = locale === 'es';
const root = es ? '/es/' : '/';
const disciplines = ['Brand Strategy','Information Architecture','UX / UI','Digital Product','Design Systems','Commerce'];
const principles = [
  ['01','Clarity before decoration','Technical information should be easy to scan.'],
  ['02','Status must be visible','Active, secure, deployed and available should feel immediate.'],
  ['03','Complexity needs hierarchy','Advanced systems can remain powerful without looking chaotic.'],
  ['04','One language across the business','Marketing, product and support should feel like parts of the same company.']
];
const sections = [
  ['Launch','Managed infrastructure for websites and digital businesses.'],
  ['Sell','Commerce infrastructure designed around reliability and growth.'],
  ['Scale','Cloud resources that expand with demand.'],
  ['Protect','Security, certificates, backups and monitoring.'],
  ['Build','Custom software and digital products.']
];
---
<BaseLayout locale={locale} title="OK Hosting — Infrastructure, made understandable" description="A retrospective product, UX and brand systems case study for OK Hosting.">
<article class="okx">
  <header class="okx-hero okx-wrap">
    <a class="okx-back" href={`${root}#projects`}>← {es ? 'Todos los proyectos' : 'All projects'}</a>
    <div class="okx-kicker"><span>OK HOSTING / DIGITAL TECHNOLOGY</span><span>MEXICO / 2026</span></div>
    <h1>Infrastructure,<br/><em>made understandable.</em></h1>
    <div class="okx-intro"><p>OK Hosting grew from a hosting provider into a broader technology business. As its offer expanded across infrastructure, software, security and managed services, the challenge became larger than redesigning a website: the company needed a digital language capable of organizing complexity.</p><p>This retrospective case study revisits my previous work with OK Hosting and explores how I would extend that system today across brand, product and customer experience.</p></div>
    <div class="okx-tag">Retrospective redesign / Conceptual extension</div>
  </header>

  <figure class="okx-asset okx-asset-hero okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/product-ecosystem.webp" alt="OK Hosting contemporary product ecosystem including homepage, dashboard, server configurator and system states" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption><span>2026 / RETROSPECTIVE PRODUCT EXPLORATION</span><span>WEB · PRODUCT · COMMERCE · SYSTEM</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">01</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">01 / CONTEXT</span><h2>A hosting company becoming a technology company.</h2><p>Hosting businesses tend to accumulate services faster than they accumulate clarity. Domains, shared hosting, VPS, dedicated servers, cloud infrastructure, SSL, software development, support and security may all belong to the same company, while customers arrive with much simpler questions: How do I launch my business? How do I keep my website online? How do I sell? How do I scale? Who manages this when something breaks?</p><p>The opportunity was to reorganize the experience around customer intent rather than the company's internal catalogue.</p></div></section>

  <div class="ia-map okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: crear aquí diagrama de arquitectura de información"/><div><span class="okx-label">OLD LOGIC / PRODUCT CATALOGUE</span>{['Hosting','Domains','VPS','Servers','SSL','Software','Security','Support'].map(x=><b>{x}</b>)}</div><i>→</i><div class="intent"><span class="okx-label">USER-ORIENTED LOGIC</span>{['Launch','Sell','Scale','Protect','Build','Manage'].map(x=><b>{x}</b>)}</div></div>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">02</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">02 / DESIGN PRINCIPLE</span><h2>Make infrastructure feel controllable.</h2><p>Infrastructure is largely invisible. Customers rarely see the servers, routing, databases or processes behind a digital service. What they experience instead is speed, availability, confidence and the ability to act.</p><p>The visual system translates that invisible infrastructure into a language of status, hierarchy and control. Dense technical information is paired with large typography, strict grids and a high-visibility green used as a functional signal for action, availability and system state.</p></div></section>
  <div class="principles okx-wrap">{principles.map(([n,t,d])=><article><span>{n}</span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></article>)}</div>
  <div class="system-board okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: refinar aquí operational language con tipografía Rift + Figtree"/><div class="type-spec"><small>DISPLAY / RIFT · INTERFACE / FIGTREE</small><strong>Aa</strong><span>BUILD<br/>DEPLOY<br/>SCALE</span></div><div class="colors"><i style="background:#030510;color:#f1eee6">#030510</i><i style="background:#00ddff;color:#030510">#00DDFF</i><i style="background:#7f2fea;color:#f1eee6">#7F2FEA</i><i style="background:#f1eee6;color:#030510">#F1EEE6</i></div><div class="status-set"><span class="status-operational"><i></i> OPERATIONAL</span><span class="status-active"><i></i> SSL ACTIVE</span><span class="status-deploying"><i></i> DEPLOYING</span><span class="status-warning"><i></i> ACTION REQUIRED</span></div></div>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">03</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">03 / INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE</span><h2>Start with the problem, not the server.</h2><p>Traditional hosting navigation assumes that customers already understand the technology they need. A customer-led structure reverses that logic. Instead of asking visitors to choose between technical products first, the system begins with the outcome they are trying to achieve and progressively introduces the infrastructure behind it.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/solution-finder.webp" alt="OK Hosting solution finder showing intent, project type and recommended infrastructure" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>PROPOSED SOLUTION FINDER</span><span>INTENT → PROJECT → RECOMMENDATION</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">04</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">04 / DIGITAL EXPERIENCE</span><h2>A website built around decisions.</h2><p>The marketing experience is designed to reduce the distance between a business need and a technical solution. Service pages combine outcome-oriented language with enough technical detail for experienced buyers to evaluate the product without overwhelming less technical customers.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-asset-stage okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: insertar aquí homepage final dentro del monitor"/><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/hero-scene.webp" alt="Dark faceted OK Hosting device scene prepared for the final homepage composition" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>HOMEPAGE PRESENTATION BASE</span><span>FINAL SCREEN COMPOSITING PENDING</span></figcaption></figure>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/mobile-experience.webp" alt="Four OK Hosting mobile product states: homepage, solution finder, dashboard and server status" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>RESPONSIVE PRODUCT EXPERIENCE</span><span>HOME · FINDER · ACCOUNT · SERVER STATUS</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">05</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">05 / PRODUCT DESIGN</span><h2>One interface from acquisition to operation.</h2><p>The same visual language can continue after the sale. Marketing pages introduce the service. The customer environment turns the same components into operational tools for infrastructure, billing, domains, support and account management.</p><span class="concept-chip">Conceptual product extension</span></div></section>
  <div class="dashboard okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí dashboard principal OK Hosting"/><nav><b>OK.</b><div>Overview<br/>Services<br/>Domains<br/>Billing<br/>Support</div><small>CESAR / ADMIN</small></nav><main><header><div><small>ACCOUNT OVERVIEW</small><h2>Good evening, César.</h2></div><button>Open new ticket ↗</button></header><div class="dash-status"><span><i></i> ALL SYSTEMS OPERATIONAL</span><small>UPDATED 18:42 CST</small></div><div class="dash-grid"><article class="services"><small>SERVICES / 04</small><h3>Managed WordPress</h3><p>raptoriano.com</p><span><i></i> Operational</span><hr/><h3>Cloud Server</h3><p>Production API</p><span><i></i> Operational</span></article><article><small>DOMAINS / 03</small><h3>klavstudio.com</h3><p>Renews Nov 14</p><b>Manage →</b></article><article><small>BILLING</small><h3>MX$1,899</h3><p>Upcoming / October 12</p><b>View invoices →</b></article></div></main></div>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">06</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">06 / SERVICE MANAGEMENT</span><h2>Technical depth without visual noise.</h2><p>Advanced users need specifications. Everyone else needs confidence. The interface separates operational status from configuration details, allowing both audiences to use the same environment without reducing the product to either raw technical data or oversimplified cards.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/production-api.webp" alt="OK Hosting Production API server detail with operational status, resource metrics and usage chart" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>CONCEPTUAL SERVICE MANAGEMENT</span><span>STATUS · RESOURCES · HISTORY · ACTIONS</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">07</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">07 / COMMERCE</span><h2>Configure before you buy.</h2><p>Infrastructure pricing becomes easier to understand when customers can see the relationship between requirements and cost. A configurable purchasing flow turns technical specifications into an interactive product rather than a static price table.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/server-configurator.webp" alt="OK Hosting server configurator with CPU, memory, storage, backups and monthly price" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>CONCEPTUAL SERVER CONFIGURATOR</span><span>SPECIFICATION → ESTIMATE → DEPLOYMENT</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">08</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">08 / DESIGN SYSTEM</span><h2>Designed as components, not pages.</h2><p>A digital brand becomes significantly more useful when its visual decisions are encoded into repeatable components. Typography, spacing, navigation, status, cards, pricing, forms and data visualization are treated as a shared system that can expand across future products.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/design-system.webp" alt="OK Hosting design system with color, typography, navigation, status, cards, forms and data patterns" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>2026 / PROPOSED DIGITAL SYSTEM</span><span>TOKENS · COMPONENTS · STATES · DATA</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">09</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">09 / COMMUNICATION SYSTEM</span><h2>The interface language beyond the interface.</h2><p>The system extends into the documents and communications surrounding the product: proposals, service reports, billing, sales material, technical documentation and lifecycle email. The goal is consistency across the moments where a technology company earns trust.</p></div></section>
  <div class="communications okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: diseñar aquí propuesta, cotización, reporte, factura y campaña digital"/><article class="proposal"><small>OK / PROPOSAL 026</small><h3>Managed infrastructure<br/>for Klav Studio.</h3><p>Prepared / 08.2026</p><b>Infrastructure,<br/>made understandable.</b></article><article class="report"><small>MONTHLY REPORT / AUGUST</small><h3>Infrastructure<br/>performance</h3><div><b>99.99%</b><span>UPTIME</span></div><div><b>48 ms</b><span>AVG RESPONSE</span></div></article><article class="campaign"><small>OK HOSTING / MANAGED CLOUD</small><h3>Scale without<br/>losing control.</h3><span>EXPLORE SOLUTIONS ↗</span></article></div>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">10</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">10 / SERVICE COMMUNICATION</span><h2>Every system event is part of the brand.</h2><p>Transactional communication is often one of the most frequent interactions between a technology company and its customers. Deployment confirmations, invoices, backup notifications, renewals and security alerts deserve the same hierarchy and clarity as the primary product.</p></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/system-emails.webp" alt="OK Hosting transactional system emails for success, warning, deployment, error and backup states" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>CONCEPTUAL SERVICE COMMUNICATION</span><span>SUCCESS · WARNING · DEPLOYING · ERROR · BACKUP</span></figcaption></figure>

  <section class="okx-section okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">11</div><div class="okx-copy"><span class="okx-label">11 / MOTION</span><h2>Showing infrastructure as a process.</h2><p>Small motion states make invisible operations understandable. Provisioning, configuration, deployment and system status can communicate progress without requiring users to understand the underlying infrastructure.</p></div></section>
  <div class="motion-stage okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: animar aquí estado provisioning → configuring → deploying → online (4–6 s)"/><div class="motion-track"><span>PROVISIONING</span><i></i><span>CONFIGURING</span><i></i><span>DEPLOYING</span><i></i><strong>ONLINE <b></b></strong></div></div>

  <section class="archive"><div class="okx-wrap archive-head"><div><span class="okx-label">12 / ORIGINAL ARCHIVE</span><h2>Where the project began.</h2></div><p>My work around OK Hosting spans an earlier stage of my career. The material below belongs to that original period. The system presented throughout this case study is a retrospective reinterpretation: an opportunity to revisit the same company with the product, interface and systems thinking I use today.</p></div><div class="archive-rule okx-wrap"><strong>ORIGINAL PROFESSIONAL WORK</strong><span>↔</span><strong>2026 RETROSPECTIVE EXPLORATION</strong></div><div class="archive-grid okx-wide"><img src="/projects/okhosting/OK-Hosting-Website.jpg" alt="Original OK Hosting website design archive" loading="lazy"/><img src="/projects/okhosting/screens/brand.webp" alt="Original OK Hosting brand work archive" loading="lazy"/><img src="/projects/okhosting/screens/mockuMagazine.webp" alt="Original OK Hosting printed work archive" loading="lazy"/></div></section>

  <section class="reflection okx-wrap"><div class="okx-number">13</div><div><span class="okx-label">13 / REFLECTION</span><h2>A brand can become infrastructure too.</h2><p>Revisiting OK Hosting years later changes the scale of the problem. What originally appeared primarily as a communication challenge can now be understood as a systems problem: many services, many customer states and many technical interactions competing for clarity.</p><p>The strongest opportunity is therefore not a new visual identity in isolation. It is a shared language connecting the company, its products and the people using them.</p><div class="cap-list">{disciplines.map(x=><span>{x}</span>)}</div><small>Original professional work + 2026 retrospective conceptual development.</small></div></section>
  <figure class="okx-asset okx-asset-final okx-wide"><DesignTodo note="CÉSAR: insertar aquí dashboard, homepage, mobile y documentos finales en los dispositivos"/><img src="/projects/okhosting/2026/final-scene.webp" alt="OK Hosting final ecosystem scene prepared for final interface compositing" loading="lazy"/><figcaption><span>FINAL ECOSYSTEM BASE</span><span>FINAL SCREEN COMPOSITING PENDING</span></figcaption></figure>
  <a class="okx-next okx-wrap" href={`${root}project/firstchoice/`}><span>NEXT PROJECT</span><strong>1st Choice CE</strong><b>↗</b></a>
</article>
</BaseLayout>
